2026-07-22 [claude-code] **Release chain: merged is not deployed — five PRs landed on main 07-21, none reached production.**

- Root cause: merges performed by the Actions app via `GITHUB_TOKEN` do not trigger workflow runs, so the push to main built nothing. `strict` required checks compounded it — each merge left every other enrolled PR `behind`, so nothing could land while main kept moving.
- `post-merge-release.yml` was written to fix this by dispatching on `pull_request_target: closed`, and never fired once — that event is suppressed by the same token rule. DELETED rather than kept: dead machinery that looks like a safety net gets counted as coverage.
- Replaced by `release-reconcile.yml` (#1499, corrected in #1500): every 15m asks whether a successful `Deploy prod` run on main contains the last release-relevant commit (paths read from build-image.yml, ancestry not equality), and dispatches build-image on drift. `schedule` is GitHub-driven, so no token can suppress it. A broken chain stays broken; a loop heals.
- Codex review found two real defects: the first loop asked about image BUILDS not DEPLOYS (a build can succeed while deploy/canary fails or auto-rolls-back, and the runs query was never filtered to main), and `pr-scope-guard.yml`'s "fail closed on truncation" comment was false — the files API caps at 3000 and reports nothing when it truncates. Both fixed in #1500.
- Durable rule landed: AGENTS.md Hard Rule 14 — verify the deployed sha, never infer it from a merge. `get_status` -> `release_state.git_sha` is the live answer.
- Live check at time of writing: prod `git_sha` 1605349e (#1498), deployed 2026-07-22T01:11Z, canary passed — genuinely in sync, since the three later commits (#1499/#1500/#1489) touch no release path.

